values ('d5e6f7a8-9b0c-4d12-9f22-2a3b4c5d6e12', 'music-history-iii-20th-c-contemporary', 'Music History III (20th C.-Contemporary)', 'Music History III surveys twentieth-century and contemporary music across modernism, experimentalism, jazz, American music, electronic media, minimalism, popular music, global contemporary traditions, and twenty-first-century practice. The course treats scores, recordings, archives, technologies, institutions, scenes, and media circulation as historical evidence. Students learn to analyze music whose forms may be tonal, atonal, serial, improvised, process-based, electronic, multimedia, popular, global, or community-based. The course asks not only what changed after 1900, but how modern musical histories are made, mediated, contested, and revised.');

