ing and Analysis Across Media", "children": [{"id": "bea72583-c203-4aab-8a78-6708f5d6f8da", "type": "concept", "title": "Score analysis, spectrograms, transcription, and close listening"}, {"id": "970a5c54-13c4-461d-86cb-3efa41338413", "type": "concept", "title": "Production analysis and sound studies"}, {"id": "66db56f4-b341-4708-a530-2e641cf06ac6", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied, social, and ecological listening"}], "description": "Students learn to choose analytical tools that fit the music."}, {"id": "692c023e-cc7d-4047-b414-13a6bb5fd12c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Primary Sources and Field Methods", "children": [{"id": "ecdfe658-0189-4bdf-bf45-c5cf99bd0c69", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, oral history, program notes, reviews, and digital traces"}, {"id": "3b5eabaa-20d9-464b-88b2-1efac75dfc3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics, consent, representation, and positionality"}, {"id": "04e3481b-79c1-4436-a07a-a96981f26931", "type": "concept", "title": "Archiving ephemeral and online materials"}], "description": "The unit trains students to work responsibly with living cultures and recent histories."}, {"id": "4638505b-c3a5-4365-9281-8f5832a4966d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historiography and Curriculum Repair", "children": [{"id": "9cafa1ae-8100-4dc8-b3a3-1590332e5694", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernism, postmodernism, and period labels"}, {"id": "266d6ed0-c4ed-4512-b3d1-df65385d1668", "type": "concept", "title": "Canon gaps and institutional power"}, {"id": "005f2bed-2aa4-422a-a68c-502d3bad0ecc", "type": "concept", "title": "Designing inclusive listening lists and research questions"}], "description": "Students critique survey narratives and build better ones."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$mh3json$::jsonb,
